From a44607ac8289a6b6e4a4a2bb320864113b8f841c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Terrydaktal <9lewis9@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 05:31:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add experimental query-isolated M8 attention with shared KV
 reads

Preserve each query's serial softmax and merge decisions while sharing KV loads across the eight verification rows. Replace wave-wide decision coupling with per-query six-head ballots, split row groups at the 16-token boundary and retain query-specific causal merge extents.

Publish the qualified downstream transformer, ABI wrapper and native probe beside the generated experimental translation unit. Add source-bound current-header compilation and its recorded successful CPU-only build, with explicit separation from the completed pinned downstream GPU checks. Keep the production dispatcher unchanged until the new header binding and full integration are qualified.

Validation: current-header HIP compilation passed without GPU execution; generated source and copied helper identities verified; no private traces or binaries included. The separate pinned implementation passed 192 query positions, causal interventions and graph checks, and was part of the completed 10K compiled model comparison.
Signed-off-by: Terrydaktal <9lewis9@gmail.com>
