+# Query-isolated M8 attention with shared KV reads
+
+Eight queries can share KV reads while retaining each query's serial softmax
+rescaling and split/merge decisions. The existing wave-wide ballot lets another
+query change those decisions, introducing a different arithmetic path.
+
+This experimental translation unit gives each query its own six-head ballot,
+groups rows at the 16-token tile boundary and uses that query's causal context
+in the merge. It retains the serial dot-product/reduction expressions. The
+existing public dispatcher is not changed.
+
+```text
+experimental/m1_m8/
+├── shared_attention.hip              # generated candidate and explicit C entry point
+├── build.py                         # source-bound current-header compilation
+├── BUILD_INPUTS.json                 # exact compilation input hashes
+├── build_stock_m1_attention_shared.py # preserved qualified-source transformer
+├── stock_m1_attention_shared.py       # qualified ABI and tensor admission wrapper
+├── probe_stock_m1_attention_shared.py # exact output, causality, guards and graph probe
+└── SOURCE_PROVENANCE.json            # downstream source identities
+```
+
+From the repository root, compile on a machine with ROCm:
+
+```sh
+uv run --no-project python experimental/m1_m8/build.py --output /tmp/r4d-shared-m8
+```
+
+The output directory must be new. Compilation produces `candidate.so`,
+`compiler.log` and `build.json`, marked `BUILT_UNTESTED`. It does not launch GPU
+kernels. The admitted candidate geometry is one sequence, eight queries, 24 Q
+heads, four KV heads, width 256, 16-token blocks and 32 splits, with BF16 or FP8
+KV. The caller owns valid block mappings, buffer sizes and stream ordering.
+
+The preserved native probe requires the pinned Radiance environment, the support
+package in [Radiance #10](https://github.com/magiccodingman/vllm-radiance/pull/10),
+its authenticated native specification and original build receipt. Run the
+source-bound builder before that probe; use its `--help` for the required paths.
+GPU execution requires explicit `--allow-gpu` and the shared qualification lease.
+The new `build.py` receipt cannot be substituted for the original qualification
+receipt: the current `r4d.h` differs, even though the attention translation unit
+and arithmetic helper headers match the measured build.
+
+The pinned downstream experiment checked 192 query positions across eight
+context boundaries and three cache storage layouts with zero mismatches,
+future-query interventions and graph replay. Its 60K FP8 layer measurement was
+0.997 ms for separate serial-query work versus 0.243 ms sharing KV reads. The
+complete compiled integration subsequently passed 10,000 aligned M1/M8 positions.
+These are completed downstream measurements, not results for this new header
+binding. Current-header execution and public-dispatch integration remain open.
+
+[Report, exact scope and compiled stage table](https://github.com/Terrydaktal/qwen-r9700-lab/releases/tag/d7-report-v1.0.0).
